      explanation: "Each a pushes an A (the first a also keeps ⊥ below), so after m a's the stack holds m A's above ⊥. Each b at state s or p pops one A, and reaching q (which empties the rest of the stack by ε-moves) requires at least one A left to pop into p via ε/A/ε — the ε-move from s to q also needs at least one A on the stack, forcing m ≥ 1 and n < m for acceptance by empty stack."
